+If no config file is given, \fBlogrotate\fR selects the first existing file
+from \fI/etc/logrotate.conf\fR, \fI/run/logrotate.conf\fR, and
+\fI/usr/lib/logrotate.conf\fR.  When that file includes
+\fI/etc/logrotate.d\fR, \fBlogrotate\fR merges files by basename from
+\fI/etc/logrotate.d\fR, \fI/run/logrotate.d\fR, and
+\fI/usr/lib/logrotate.d\fR in the same priority order.  A higher-priority
+empty file masks a lower file with the same basename.  If any errors occur
+while rotating logs, \fBlogrotate\fR will exit with non-zero status, although
+the state file will be updated.
 
